```

## Retrieval order

1. Scoped ranked search against the `{{SEARCH_COLLECTION}}` collection alone; confirm every returned path starts with `{{SEARCH_COLLECTION}}/`. Read the top three to five pages, Concept pages first.
2. Read this index for the neighbours the query missed; the claim, source and use cells say which pages to open.
3. On the chosen Concept page, read `## Source evidence` to find which raw chapters back the claim and which challenge it.
4. Read the relevant raw chapters under `raw/Books/<Book>/` for direct quotes and dated episodes.
5. Open `raw/images/` files when a chapter references a diagram.
6. Use `Routes/` for audit sequence and output shape.
7. Label coverage limits for current facts, valuation, legal, security, safety-critical, and current AI capability questions. When QMD was unavailable and step 1 fell back to this index, say so in the output.
